IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`
IMPORT `wra2-s46-jsa-sanctions`
IMPORT `wra2-s54-esa-commitment`

-- wra2-s57-esa-requirements.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) s 57, claimant responsibilities for employment and support allowance after the introduction of universal credit.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part wra2. Host Act short name: WRA2007 = Welfare Reform Act 2007; ESA = employment and support allowance.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt (a converter script's plain-text rendering; not the official text).
-- Section 57 substitutes WRA2007 ss 11 to 16: work-related requirements (11 to 11I), sanctions (11J), delegation (11K); adds definitions to WRA2007 s 24
-- and paragraphs 10ZA and 10B to Schedule 2. It reuses the three-valued logic helpers of the s 46 module.
-- Mapping to the core (seam 9 of PLAN.md): WRA2007 11J -> `employment and support allowance sanction`.
-- ESA has only TWO work-related requirements (WFI and WPR), so only two of the core's `Work-related requirement` constructors apply.
-- Seam 1 of PLAN.md: "single person" borrows s 39(1) of Part 1 (wra1's range); the answer is taken as the input `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple`.

§ `s 57 WRA2007 11: work-related requirements`

-- src:965 | (1) The following provisions of this Part provide for the Secretary of State to impose work-related requirements with which persons entitled to an employment and support allowance must comply for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11(1) (src:965)
GIVEN `a work-related requirement has been imposed on the person entitled to an employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11(1) the person must comply with the work-related requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a work-related requirement has been imposed on the person entitled to an employment and support allowance`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provisions "provide for the Secretary of State to impose work-related requirements with which persons entitled to an employment and support allowance must comply"; none has been imposed
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11 what a requirement asks of the person` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11B(1) to participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(1) to take particular action specified by the Secretary of State to make paid work more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11 to do something else`

-- src:983 | (1) In this Part a “work-focused interview requirement” is a requirement that a person participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11B(1) (src:983)
GIVEN `what the requirement asks` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11 what a requirement asks of the person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11B(1) the requirement is a work-focused interview requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “work-focused interview requirement” is a requirement that a person participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State" (a definition; "is", not "means", see NOTES)
    `what the requirement asks` EQUALS `s 57 WRA2007 11B(1) to participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State`

-- src:988 | (1) In this Part a “work preparation requirement” is a requirement that a person take particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose of making it more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the person will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work).
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11C(1) (src:988)
GIVEN `what the requirement asks` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11 what a requirement asks of the person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11C(1) the requirement is a work preparation requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “work preparation requirement” is a requirement that a person take particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose of making it more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the person will obtain paid work"
    `what the requirement asks` EQUALS `s 57 WRA2007 11C(1) to take particular action specified by the Secretary of State to make paid work more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State`

-- src:966 | (2) In this Part “work-related requirement” means—
-- src:967 | (a) a work-focused interview requirement (see section 11B);
-- src:968 | (b) a work preparation requirement (see section 11C).
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11(2) (src:966-968)
GIVEN `what the requirement asks` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11 what a requirement asks of the person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11(2) the requirement is a work-related requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“work-related requirement” means (a) a work-focused interview requirement ... (b) a work preparation requirement"
        `s 57 WRA2007 11B(1) the requirement is a work-focused interview requirement` `what the requirement asks`
    OR  `s 57 WRA2007 11C(1) the requirement is a work preparation requirement` `what the requirement asks`

-- src:966 | (2) In this Part “work-related requirement” means—
-- src:967 | (a) a work-focused interview requirement (see section 11B);
-- src:968 | (b) a work preparation requirement (see section 11C).
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11(2) (src:966-968)
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `Work-related requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11(2) the requirement is one of the work-related requirements of this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement`
    WHEN `work-focused interview requirement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `work preparation requirement` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“work-related requirement” means (a) ... (b) ..." -- a work search requirement is not one of the two
    WHEN `work search requirement` THEN FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“work-related requirement” means (a) ... (b) ..." -- a work availability requirement is not one of the two
    WHEN `work availability requirement` THEN FALSE

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11(3) group` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11(3)(a) persons subject to no work-related requirements (see section 11D)`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11(3)(b) persons subject to work-focused interview requirement only (see section 11E)`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11(3)(c) persons subject to work-focused interview and work preparation requirements (see section 11F)`

-- src:969 | (3) The work-related requirements which may be imposed on a person depend on which of the following groups the person falls into—
-- src:970 | (a) persons subject to no work-related requirements (see section 11D);
-- src:971 | (b) persons subject to work-focused interview requirement only (see section 11E);
-- src:972 | (c) persons subject to work-focused interview and work preparation requirements (see section 11F).
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11(3) (src:969-972)
GIVEN `the group` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11(3) group`
GIVETH A `Group of claimants by requirement`
`s 57 WRA2007 11(3) the core's group of claimants by requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the group`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11(3)(a) persons subject to no work-related requirements (see section 11D)` THEN `no work-related requirements`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11(3)(b) persons subject to work-focused interview requirement only (see section 11E)` THEN `work-focused interview requirement only`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11(3)(c) persons subject to work-focused interview and work preparation requirements (see section 11F)` THEN `work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only`

§ `s 57 WRA2007 11A: claimant commitment`

-- src:974 | (1) A claimant commitment is a record of the responsibilities of a person entitled to an employment and support allowance in relation to the award of the allowance.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11A(1) (src:974)
GIVEN `the document is a record of the responsibilities of a person entitled to an employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the award the record is in relation to` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11A(1) the document is a claimant commitment` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is a record of the responsibilities of a person entitled to an employment and support allowance in relation to the award of the allowance" (a definition; "is", not "means", see NOTES)
        `the document is a record of the responsibilities of a person entitled to an employment and support allowance`
    AND `s 54 WRA2007 1C(1) the award is an award of an employment and support allowance` `the award the record is in relation to`

-- src:975 | (2) A claimant commitment is to be prepared by the Secretary of State and may be reviewed and updated as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
-- src:1086 | (1) The functions of the Secretary of State under sections 11 to 11I may be exercised by, or by the employees of, such person as the Secretary of State may authorise for the purpose (an “authorised person”).
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11A(2) with 11K(1) (src:975 src:1086)
GIVEN `who prepared the claimant commitment` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11A(2) the claimant commitment was prepared by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who prepared the claimant commitment`
    WHEN `the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- WRA2007 11K(1): the functions of the Secretary of State under sections 11 to 11I may be exercised by an authorised person
    WHEN `an authorised person` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is to be prepared by the Secretary of State" says nothing of preparation by anyone else
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:976 | (3) A claimant commitment is to be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11A(3) (src:976)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State thinks the form fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11A(3) the claimant commitment is in the form the Secretary of State thinks fit` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is to be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit"
    `the Secretary of State thinks the form fit`

-- src:977 | (4) A claimant commitment is to include—
-- src:978 | (a) a record of the requirements that the person must comply with under this Part (or such of them as the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include),
-- src:979 | (b) any prescribed information, and
-- src:980 | (c) any other information the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11A(4) (src:977-980)
GIVEN `it includes a record of the requirements the person must comply with, or of such of them as the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes the prescribed information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it includes any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11A(4) the claimant commitment includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is to include (a) a record of the requirements that the person must comply with under this Part"
        IF NOT `it includes a record of the requirements the person must comply with, or of such of them as the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is to include ... (c) any other information the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include"
        IF NOT `it includes any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `it includes the prescribed information`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any prescribed information"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what information is prescribed is left to regulations
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:981 | (5) For the purposes of this Part a person accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it in such manner as may be prescribed.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11A(5) (src:981)
GIVEN `the person accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11A(5) the person accepts the claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it"
        IF NOT `the person accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the person accepted it in the manner prescribed`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if, ... accepts ... in such manner as may be prescribed" -- accepted, but not in the prescribed manner
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the manner of acceptance is prescribed in regulations that are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `s 57 WRA2007 11B and 11C: the two requirements`

-- src:984 | (2) A work-focused interview is an interview for prescribed purposes relating to work or work preparation.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11B(2) (src:984)
GIVEN `the interview is for prescribed purposes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the purposes relate to work or work preparation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11B(2) the interview is a work-focused interview` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A work-focused interview is an interview for prescribed purposes relating to work or work preparation"
        IF NOT `the purposes relate to work or work preparation`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which purposes are prescribed is left to regulations
        OTHERWISE `the interview is for prescribed purposes`

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11B(3) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11B(3) making it more likely, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, that the person will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work)`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11B(3) some other purpose`

-- src:985 | (3) The purposes which may be prescribed under subsection (2) include in particular that of making it more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the person will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work).
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11B(3) (src:985)
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11B(3) purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11B(3) the purpose may be prescribed under subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11B(3) making it more likely, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, that the person will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The purposes which may be prescribed ... include in particular" one purpose and do not close the list
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) how the interview is to take place`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) when the interview is to take place`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) where the interview is to take place`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) some other matter`

-- src:986 | (4) The Secretary of State may specify how, when and where a work-focused interview is to take place.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) (src:986)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) the Secretary of State may specify that matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) how the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) when the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11B(4) where the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "how, when and where" are the matters the Secretary of State may specify
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:989 | (2) The Secretary of State may under subsection (1) specify the time to be devoted to any particular action.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11C(2) (src:989)
GIVEN `the matter is the time to be devoted to a particular action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11C(2) the Secretary of State may specify the time to be devoted to the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is the time to be devoted to a particular action`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "the time to be devoted to any particular action" and says nothing of other matters
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(a) attending a skills assessment`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(b) improving personal presentation`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(c) participating in training`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(d) participating in an employment programme`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(e) undertaking work experience or a work placement`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(f) developing a business plan`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(g) any action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1)`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(4) taking part in a work-focused health-related assessment`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3) some other action`

-- src:990 | (3) Action which may be specified under subsection (1) includes in particular—
-- src:991 | (a) attending a skills assessment;
-- src:992 | (b) improving personal presentation;
-- src:993 | (c) participating in training;
-- src:994 | (d) participating in an employment programme;
-- src:995 | (e) undertaking work experience or a work placement;
-- src:996 | (f) developing a business plan;
-- src:997 | (g) any action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1).
-- src:998 | (4) The action which may be specified under subsection (1) includes taking part in a work-focused health-related assessment.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11C(3) with 11C(4) (src:990-998)
GIVEN `the action` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3) action`
      `the action is prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11C(3) the action may be specified under subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(a) attending a skills assessment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(b) improving personal presentation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(c) participating in training` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(d) participating in an employment programme` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(e) undertaking work experience or a work placement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(f) developing a business plan` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): (g) "any action prescribed for the purpose" is prescribed in regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(3)(g) any action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1)` THEN `the action is prescribed`
    -- 11C(4): "The action which may be specified under subsection (1) includes taking part in a work-focused health-related assessment"
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(4) taking part in a work-focused health-related assessment` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Action which may be specified ... includes in particular" and does not close the list
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:999 | (5) In subsection (4) “work-focused health-related assessment” means an assessment by a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State which is carried out for the purpose of assessing—
-- src:1000 | (a) the extent to which the person's capability for work may be improved by taking steps in relation to their physical or mental condition, and
-- src:1001 | (b) such other matters relating to their physical or mental condition and the likelihood of their obtaining or remaining in work or being able to do so as may be prescribed.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11C(5) (src:999-1001)
GIVEN `the assessment is by a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carried out to assess the extent to which the person's capability for work may be improved by taking steps in relation to their physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carried out to assess such other matters as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11C(5) the assessment is a work-focused health-related assessment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“work-focused health-related assessment” means an assessment by a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State which is carried out for the purpose of assessing (a) ... and (b) ..."
        IF NOT `the assessment is by a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the extent to which the person's capability for work may be improved" -- not assessed
        IF NOT `it is carried out to assess the extent to which the person's capability for work may be improved by taking steps in relation to their physical or mental condition`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): (b) "such other matters ... as may be prescribed" are in regulations that are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE `it is carried out to assess such other matters as may be prescribed`

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6) kind of professional` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6)(a) a registered medical practitioner`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6)(b) a registered nurse`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6)(c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by an Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6)(d) a member of another profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6) some other kind of professional`

-- src:1002 | (6) In subsection (5) “health care professional” means—
-- src:1003 | (a) a registered medical practitioner,
-- src:1004 | (b) a registered nurse,
-- src:1005 | (c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by an Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999, or
-- src:1006 | (d) a member of such other profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002 as may be prescribed.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11C(6) (src:1002-1006)
GIVEN `the professional` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6) kind of professional`
      `the profession is prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11C(6) the professional is a health care professional` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the professional`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6)(a) a registered medical practitioner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6)(b) a registered nurse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6)(c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by an Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): (d) "such other profession ... as may be prescribed"; the regulations are not among the sources
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11C(6)(d) a member of another profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002` THEN `the profession is prescribed`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“health care professional” means" the four kinds listed
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 57 WRA2007 24: the terms the section adds`

-- src:1108 | “child” means a person under the age of 16;
@ref s 57(4)(a) WRA2007 24(1) child (src:1108)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) the person is a child` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“child” means a person under the age of 16"
    (`the person`'s `age in years`) LESS THAN 16

-- src:1109 | “single person” means an individual who is not a member of a couple (within the meaning of Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012);
@ref s 57(4)(a) WRA2007 24(1) single person (src:1109)
GIVEN `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) the person is a single person` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“single person” means an individual who is not a member of a couple (within the meaning of Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012)"
    NOT `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple`

-- src:1110 | “work” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
@ref s 57(4)(a) WRA2007 24(1) work (src:1110)
GIVEN `the activity is work as regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) the activity is work` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "“work” has such meaning as may be prescribed"; the regulations are not among the sources
    `the activity is work as regulations prescribe`

DECLARE `s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) term` IS ONE OF
    `s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) work-focused interview requirement`
    `s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) work preparation requirement`
    `s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) work-related requirement`

-- src:1111 | “work-focused interview requirement” has the meaning given by section 11B;
-- src:1112 | “work preparation requirement” has the meaning given by section 11C;
-- src:1113 | “work-related requirement” has the meaning given by section 11;
@ref s 57(4)(a) WRA2007 24(1) pointers (src:1111-1113)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) the section that gives the meaning of the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) work-focused interview requirement` THEN "11B"
    WHEN `s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) work preparation requirement` THEN "11C"
    WHEN `s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) work-related requirement` THEN "11"

-- src:1114 | (b) for the definition of “work-related activity” there is substituted—
-- src:1115 | “work-related activity”, in relation to a person, means activity which makes it more likely that the person will obtain or remain in work or be able to do so;
@ref s 57(4)(b) WRA2007 24(1) work-related activity (src:1114-1115)
GIVEN `the activity makes it more likely that the person will obtain work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity makes it more likely that the person will remain in work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity makes it more likely that the person will be able to obtain or remain in work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(4)(b) WRA2007 24(1) the activity is work-related activity` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“work-related activity”, in relation to a person, means activity which makes it more likely that the person will obtain or remain in work or be able to do so"
        `the activity makes it more likely that the person will obtain work`
    OR  `the activity makes it more likely that the person will remain in work`
    OR  `the activity makes it more likely that the person will be able to obtain or remain in work`

-- src:1129 | (8) In that Schedule, after paragraph 10A there is inserted—
-- src:1130 | 10B Responsibility for children
-- src:1131 | Regulations may for any purpose of this Part specify circumstances in which a person is or is not responsible for a child.
@ref s 57(8) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 10B (src:1129-1131)
GIVEN `regulations specify circumstances in which the person is or is not responsible for the child, and these are they` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(8) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 10B the person is responsible for the child` MEANS
