§ `s 57 WRA2007 11E: persons subject to work-focused interview requirement only`

-- src:1019 | (1) A person falls within this section if—
-- src:1020 | (a) the person is a single person responsible for a child who is aged at least 1 and is under a prescribed age (which may not be less than 3), or
-- src:1021 | (b) the person is of a prescribed description.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11E(1) (src:1019-1021)
GIVEN `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations specify circumstances in which the person is or is not responsible for the child, and these are they` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the age of the child in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age that regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the person is of a description prescribed for section 11E(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11E(1) the person falls within section 11E` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person falls within this section if (a) ... or (b) ..." -- neither holds (a failed "if", reading (a) of NOTES)
    `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` `limb (a)` `the person is of a description prescribed for section 11E(1)(b)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST (`s 57(4) WRA2007 24(1) the person is a single person` `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple`)) (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (`s 57(8) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 10B the person is responsible for the child` `regulations specify circumstances in which the person is or is not responsible for the child, and these are they`) `the child is at least 1 and under the prescribed age`)
        `the child is at least 1 and under the prescribed age` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the age that regulations prescribe`
            WHEN JUST prescribed THEN
                BRANCH
                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a prescribed age (which may not be less than 3)" -- a lower age is outside what the subsection allows
                    IF prescribed LESS THAN 3
                    THEN NOTHING
                    OTHERWISE JUST (`the age of the child in years` AT LEAST 1 AND `the age of the child in years` LESS THAN prescribed)
            -- the age is prescribed in regulations that are not among the sources, but line 1020 bounds it: "a prescribed age (which may not be less than 3)", so every age the regulations may prescribe is at least 3
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                BRANCH
                    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a child who is aged at least 1" (line 1020) -- a child under 1 is not aged at least 1, whatever age is prescribed
                    IF `the age of the child in years` LESS THAN 1
                    THEN JUST FALSE
                    -- "a child who ... is under a prescribed age (which may not be less than 3)" (line 1020) -- a child aged 1 or 2 is under every age that may be prescribed
                    IF `the age of the child in years` LESS THAN 3
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a child aged 3 or more is under the prescribed age only if the prescribed age is above the child's age, and that age is in regulations that are not among the sources
                    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1022 | (2) The Secretary of State may, subject to this Part, impose a work-focused interview requirement on a person entitled to an employment and support allowance who falls within this section.
