-- src:1047 | (5) Regulations must make provision to secure that, in prescribed circumstances, where a person has recently been a victim of domestic violence—
-- src:1049 | (b) the Secretary of State may not impose any other requirement on that person during that period.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11H(5)(b) (src:1047 src:1049)
GIVEN `the person has recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in prescribed circumstances` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day is within the period of 13 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11H(5)(b) the Secretary of State may impose another requirement on the person that day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the person has recently been a victim of domestic violence`
           AND `the person is in prescribed circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the day is within the period of 13 weeks`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary of State may not impose any other requirement on the person during that period"
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a person who has recently been a victim, in prescribed circumstances, during the 13 weeks only
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1050 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5)—
-- src:1051 | (a) “domestic violence“ has such meaning as may be prescribed;
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11H(6)(a) (src:1050-1051)
GIVEN `the meaning regulations prescribe for "domestic violence" fits the facts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11H(6)(a) the conduct is domestic violence` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "“domestic violence“ has such meaning as may be prescribed"; the regulations are not among the sources
    `the meaning regulations prescribe for "domestic violence" fits the facts`

-- src:1052 | (b) “victim of domestic violence” means a person on or against whom domestic violence is inflicted or threatened (and regulations under subsection (5) may prescribe circumstances in which a person is to be treated as being or not being a victim of domestic violence);
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11H(6)(b) (src:1052)
GIVEN `domestic violence is inflicted on or against the person, or threatened` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations treat the person as being or not being a victim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11H(6)(b) the person is a victim of domestic violence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations treat the person as being or not being a victim`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (supplied): regulations under subsection (5) prescribe circumstances in which a person is to be treated as not being a victim
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- "means a person on or against whom domestic violence is inflicted or threatened"; whether the conduct is domestic violence is undefined (6H(6)(a)), so the answer follows that input
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `domestic violence is inflicted on or against the person, or threatened`

-- src:1053 | (c) a person has recently been a victim of domestic violence if a prescribed period has not expired since the violence was inflicted or threatened.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11H(6)(c) (src:1053)
GIVEN `the date of the question` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the prescribed period since the violence was inflicted or threatened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11H(6)(c) the person has recently been a victim of domestic violence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the prescribed period since the violence was inflicted or threatened`
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the date of the question` AT MOST lastday
            THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has recently been a victim of domestic violence if a prescribed period has not expired since the violence was inflicted or threatened" -- the period has expired (a failed "if", reading (a) of NOTES)
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed period is in regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1055 | Regulations may make provision as to circumstances in which a person is to be treated as having—
