    `regulations treat the person as having complied`

§ `s 57 WRA2007 11J: sanctions`

-- src:1059 | (1) The amount of an award of an employment and support allowance is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure by a person which is sanctionable under this section.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11J(1) (src:1059)
GIVETH A `Provision that reduces an award`
`s 57 WRA2007 11J the provision that reduces an award` MEANS `employment and support allowance sanction`

-- src:1060 | (2) It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a person—
-- src:1061 | (a) fails for no good reason to comply with a work-related requirement;
-- src:1062 | (b) fails for no good reason to comply with a requirement under section 11G.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11J(2) (src:1060-1062)
GIVEN `the person failed to comply with a work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with a requirement under section 11G` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had a good reason` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11J(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 11J` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a person -- (a) fails for no good reason to comply with a work-related requirement; (b) fails for no good reason to comply with a requirement under section 11G" -- neither limb holds (a failed "if", reading (a) of NOTES)
    `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both`
        (JUST (`the person failed to comply with a work-related requirement` OR `the person failed to comply with a requirement under section 11G`))
        (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the person had a good reason`)

-- src:1059 | (1) The amount of an award of an employment and support allowance is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure by a person which is sanctionable under this section.
-- src:1081 | (8) Regulations may provide—
-- src:1082 | (a) for cases in which no reduction is to be made under this section;
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11J(1) with 11J(8)(a) (src:1059 src:1081-1082)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 11J` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in the case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11J(1) the award is to be reduced in accordance with section 11J` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure by a person which is sanctionable under this section" -- there is no such failure
        IF `the failure is sanctionable under section 11J` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the failure is sanctionable under section 11J` EQUALS NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether there is a sanctionable failure is not known
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in the case`
            -- FALSE-kind (supplied): regulations under 11J(8)(a) provide for cases in which no reduction is to be made
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulations under 11J(8)(a) are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1063 | (3) Regulations are to specify—
-- src:1064 | (a) the amount of a reduction under this section, and
-- src:1065 | (b) the period for which such a reduction has effect.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11J(3)(a) with (b) (src:1063-1065)
GIVEN `the award before the reduction, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57 WRA2007 11J(3)(a) the award after the reduction, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds`
    WHEN JUST reduction THEN
        BRANCH
            IF reduction AT MOST `the award before the reduction, in pounds`
            THEN JUST (`the award before the reduction, in pounds` MINUS reduction)
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what happens when the reduction is more than the award
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations are to specify the amount of a reduction"; they are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4) kind of period` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4)(a) a period continuing until the person meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4)(b) a fixed period not exceeding 26 weeks`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4)(c) a combination of both`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4) some other period`

-- src:1066 | (4) Regulations under subsection (3)(b) may provide that a reduction under this section in relation to any failure is to have effect for—
-- src:1067 | (a) a period continuing until the person meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State,
-- src:1068 | (b) a fixed period not exceeding 26 weeks which is—
-- src:1069 | (i) specified in the regulations, or
-- src:1070 | (ii) determined in any case by the Secretary of State, or
-- src:1071 | (c) a combination of both.
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11J(4) (src:1066-1071)
GIVEN `the period` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4) kind of period`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11J(4) regulations may provide that the reduction has effect for that kind of period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4)(a) a period continuing until the person meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4)(b) a fixed period not exceeding 26 weeks` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4)(c) a combination of both` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the regulations "may provide that a reduction ... is to have effect for" the three kinds listed
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11J(4) some other period` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1066 | (4) Regulations under subsection (3)(b) may provide that a reduction under this section in relation to any failure is to have effect for—
-- src:1068 | (b) a fixed period not exceeding 26 weeks which is—
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11J(4)(b) (src:1066 src:1068)
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11J(4)(b) the fixed period of the reduction is within 26 weeks` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fixed period not exceeding 26 weeks" -- 26 weeks is 182 days, both days counting
    ((Day `the last day of the reduction` MINUS Day `the first day of the reduction`) PLUS 1) AT MOST 182

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11J(5) kind of condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(5)(a) a condition that the failure ceases`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(5)(b) a condition relating to future compliance with a work-related requirement or a requirement under section 11G`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(5) some other condition`

