GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11K(2) an authorisation given by virtue of the section may authorise the exercise of a function in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    -- "An authorisation given by virtue of this section may authorise the exercise of a function -- (a) wholly or to a limited extent; (b) generally or in particular cases or areas; (c) unconditionally or subject to conditions"
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(2)(a) an authorisation wholly` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(2)(a) an authorisation to a limited extent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(2)(b) an authorisation generally` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(2)(b) an authorisation in particular cases or areas` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(2)(c) an authorisation unconditionally` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(2)(c) an authorisation subject to conditions` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names three pairs and says nothing of any other way of limiting an authorisation
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(2) some other kind of authorisation` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3) term or effect` IS ONE OF
    `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3)(a) the authorisation specifies its duration`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3)(b) the authorisation is varied or revoked at any time`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3)(c) the authorisation prevents the Secretary of State or another person from exercising the function to which it relates`
    `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3) some other term or effect`

-- src:1091 | (3) An authorisation under this section—
-- src:1092 | (a) may specify its duration;
-- src:1093 | (b) may be varied or revoked at any time by the Secretary of State;
-- src:1094 | (c) does not prevent the Secretary of State or another person from exercising the function to which the authorisation relates.
