GIVEN `the term or effect` IS A `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3) term or effect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11K(3) an authorisation under the section may have this term or effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term or effect`
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3)(a) the authorisation specifies its duration` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3)(b) the authorisation is varied or revoked at any time` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An authorisation under this section ... (c) does not prevent the Secretary of State or another person from exercising the function to which the authorisation relates"
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3)(c) the authorisation prevents the Secretary of State or another person from exercising the function to which it relates` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection lists three things about an authorisation and says nothing of any other term or effect
    WHEN `s 57 WRA2007 11K(3) some other term or effect` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1093 | (b) may be varied or revoked at any time by the Secretary of State;
@ref s 57 WRA2007 11K(3)(b) (src:1093)
GIVEN `who varies or revokes the authorisation` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 WRA2007 11K(3)(b) the authorisation may be varied or revoked at any time by this person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who varies or revokes the authorisation`
    WHEN `the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may be varied or revoked at any time by the Secretary of State" says nothing of anyone else
