§ `s 57(7) WRA2007 Schedule 2: good reason`

-- src:1122 | 10ZA
-- src:1123 | Regulations may for any purpose of this Part provide for—
-- src:1124 | (a) circumstances in which a person is to be treated as having or not having a good reason for an act or omission;
-- src:1125 | (b) matters which are or are not to be taken into account in determining whether a person has a good reason for an act or omission.
@ref s 57(7)(b) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 10ZA (src:1122-1125)
GIVEN `regulations treat the person as having or not having a good reason in the circumstances` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `on the facts, taking into account the matters regulations require or forbid, the person has a good reason` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(7)(b) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 10ZA the person has a good reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations treat the person as having or not having a good reason in the circumstances`
    -- 10ZA(a): "circumstances in which a person is to be treated as having or not having a good reason for an act or omission"; treated as, so the answer follows the regulations
    WHEN JUST treated THEN JUST treated
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Act gives no test of a good reason and no regulations are among the sources; the answer follows the facts, taking into account the matters regulations require or forbid (10ZA(b))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `on the facts, taking into account the matters regulations require or forbid, the person has a good reason`
